WEBVTT

00:21.650 --> 00:23.980
Count!
What is this?

00:24.380 --> 00:26.780
I ordered a tiger!

00:27.450 --> 00:29.940
You are not satisfied with
the merchandise?

00:30.660 --> 00:31.720
Of course not!

00:31.860 --> 00:34.190
You sent me a hanging scroll with
a painting of a bamboo grove!

00:34.360 --> 00:38.090
Thanks to you, I made a complete
fool of myself in front of everyone!

00:39.600 --> 00:43.260
Then, you broke our agreement
not to show it to anybody.

00:43.970 --> 00:47.740
Yes! I held a party to
show off the tiger.

00:54.280 --> 00:55.370
Tiger?

00:56.150 --> 00:57.080
What is this?!

00:57.280 --> 00:58.720
What kind of trick is this?!

00:58.920 --> 01:00.910
Trick?
It is not a trick.

01:01.250 --> 01:03.250
That is what I promised you...

01:03.660 --> 01:06.750
the last remaining tiger
of his kind, in this world.

01:08.660 --> 01:09.860
A real tiger?!

01:10.900 --> 01:13.160
Stay away!
Don't come near me!

01:13.700 --> 01:15.690
As you breached the
term of the contract...

01:15.770 --> 01:19.400
''not to show it to anybody
under any circumstances'',...

01:20.210 --> 01:23.660
I'm afraid we cannot assume any
responsibilities for the consequences.

01:24.010 --> 01:25.700
Wait...
Wait, please!

01:25.780 --> 01:27.210
Count! Count D!

01:36.220 --> 01:39.190
Welcome to my pet shop.
I am Count D.

01:40.030 --> 01:41.390
This is Chinatown.

01:42.200 --> 01:48.100
A mysterious place with many
rare and valuable commodities.

01:49.270 --> 01:53.710
Tonight, you shall find
something you desire.

02:01.780 --> 02:02.870
Good grief!

02:03.380 --> 02:06.720
They say it looked like he'd been
attacked by a pack of wild dogs!

02:06.850 --> 02:10.290
No, I heard it must've been
something bigger than a dog.

02:10.560 --> 02:13.180
Yeah, something like
a lion or tiger.

02:13.430 --> 02:14.480
A tiger?

02:14.630 --> 02:17.290
No way! There are
no tigers in Chinatown.

02:22.470 --> 02:25.060
Please take good care of it.

02:25.200 --> 02:26.330
I will! Thank you!

02:27.970 --> 02:28.770
Hold it!

02:30.140 --> 02:31.200
Excuse me.

02:36.080 --> 02:37.570
Oh, just a normal bird...

02:40.590 --> 02:41.450
Hello.

02:46.760 --> 02:48.950
Shoot, nobody's home.

02:57.670 --> 02:59.870
You scared the heck out of me!

03:00.940 --> 03:01.840
Welcome.

03:02.710 --> 03:09.640
We have everything from dogs to cats
to birds to insects to reptiles.

03:10.450 --> 03:12.110
What can I do for you?

03:14.850 --> 03:16.850
There have been a string
of unnatural deaths.

03:17.190 --> 03:20.020
All the victims were
customers of this pet shop.

03:21.690 --> 03:26.630
I hear the pet shop is a cover and
your real business is the human trade...

03:26.700 --> 03:29.730
drug dealing, and Chinese terrorists.

03:31.300 --> 03:34.500
The pet shop is suspected
of selling animals...

03:34.570 --> 03:38.240
prohibited by the
Washington Convention.

03:39.050 --> 03:43.880
You must be mistaken.
We do not handle such species here.

03:44.550 --> 03:45.520
Shut up!

03:45.650 --> 03:47.640
It's not worth discussing with you.
Where's the owner?

03:48.150 --> 03:49.950
I'm afraid my grandfather
is out of town.

03:50.020 --> 03:51.890
I am tending the shop
in the meantime.

03:52.660 --> 03:54.650
Then tell me what you sold
to Liu Tai Wei.

03:55.530 --> 03:57.120
Don't try to deceive me.

03:57.300 --> 04:00.320
I know he frequented your shop.
Right?!

04:02.130 --> 04:05.100
Yes, we did sell him an animal.
A tiger.

04:07.010 --> 04:08.170
I knew it!

04:09.510 --> 04:11.030
If you'd like, I'll show it to you.

04:11.780 --> 04:14.840
He didn't like it
and returned it to us.

04:16.120 --> 04:17.010
What?

04:17.350 --> 04:18.480
This way, please.

04:18.550 --> 04:20.540
The only tiger we have here.

04:26.760 --> 04:28.090
What...what's this?!

04:31.960 --> 04:33.960
You bastard! You scum!

04:34.370 --> 04:36.130
You'll see me again!

04:36.200 --> 04:38.140
I'll get you next time!

04:43.940 --> 04:47.540
Your daughter...?
I'm sorry to hear that.

04:48.310 --> 04:52.180
We thought if we got a pet,
it may cheer us up a little.

04:52.790 --> 04:59.050
No, nothing can take her place.
Alice was my angel.

05:02.560 --> 05:06.050
Oh, then you will like this.

05:08.500 --> 05:10.370
Please come to the back room.

05:13.210 --> 05:14.330
This way.

05:16.910 --> 05:18.900
However, if you wish
to buy this animal,...

05:19.350 --> 05:23.580
you must agree to the term that you
will not let anyone else see her.

05:26.050 --> 05:26.980
Please come in.

05:42.100 --> 05:43.230
A...Alice?

05:44.470 --> 05:46.460
Alice, what are you doing here?

05:46.810 --> 05:48.830
Are we having a dream?

05:49.940 --> 05:53.780
No...She looks just like our Alice!

05:55.750 --> 05:58.440
Please do not be mistaken.
She is a rabbit.

05:59.990 --> 06:00.920
A rabbit?

06:01.820 --> 06:02.950
It can't be!

06:03.290 --> 06:07.020
She is a rare species inhabiting
an isolated island off of Australia.

06:07.430 --> 06:09.420
This is a pet shop.

06:10.000 --> 06:12.520
We do not sell anything but animals.

06:17.500 --> 06:19.770
Yes, of course. She is a rabbit.

06:21.970 --> 06:25.070
Please! Give us this girl...
I mean, this rabbit!

06:25.810 --> 06:26.900
Oh, please!

06:28.810 --> 06:32.440
Thank you for your business.
Please sign the contract.

06:34.490 --> 06:35.510
Of course!

06:35.820 --> 06:38.050
Now, this rabbit is yours.

06:39.130 --> 06:42.920
However, please read carefully
the three terms on the document.

06:43.530 --> 06:46.500
(1) You will not show her to anybody.

06:47.230 --> 06:50.500
(2) You will never let the incense
that comes with her, burn out.

06:51.100 --> 06:55.160
(3) You will never feed her anything
but water and fresh vegetables.

06:55.840 --> 06:57.430
Especially number three.

06:57.610 --> 07:02.980
Do not ever give her anything else,
even if she begs.

07:04.280 --> 07:06.580
If you breach any of these terms,...

07:06.690 --> 07:12.180
we cannot assume any responsibilities
for the consequences.

07:14.930 --> 07:19.360
Then, please take good care of her.

07:21.100 --> 07:23.530
Let's go, before anyone sees us.

07:30.710 --> 07:33.770
They bought something.

07:34.780 --> 07:36.340
Drugs? Or...

07:45.360 --> 07:48.450
Here, Alice.
This is your room.

07:48.690 --> 07:51.220
We kept it the way you'd left it.

07:52.800 --> 07:57.700
Yes, you have come back home.

08:09.180 --> 08:10.580
Mama...

08:11.820 --> 08:13.410
Did she say that?

08:14.150 --> 08:16.250
Mama... Mama...

08:17.520 --> 08:20.510
Yes, it's your Mama!
Alice, say it again!

08:22.030 --> 08:24.330
Mama... Mama...

08:29.600 --> 08:31.590
Da... Daddy...

08:32.600 --> 08:34.600
Oh, how can she...?
It's a miracle!

08:35.410 --> 08:38.000
Thank God.
We thank you, God.

08:39.410 --> 08:42.110
Now we can start again...

08:42.650 --> 08:44.980
...as a real family.

08:46.490 --> 08:47.920
Mama...

08:50.890 --> 08:54.790
Alice, Alice?
Where are you, honey?

08:55.290 --> 08:57.920
Oh, there you are.
Here, let's tie your hair.

08:58.130 --> 09:04.630
Your mommy bought a ribbon for you.
See, isn't it pretty? Oh, don't fidget.

09:05.640 --> 09:08.000
''Your mommy bought
a ribbon for you,'' she says.

09:09.370 --> 09:09.970
Damn it!

09:10.010 --> 09:11.700
I was sure there was something
fishy about that pet shop.

09:11.740 --> 09:16.310
Did you hear about Alice?

09:16.680 --> 09:20.950
Alice Hayward?
Didn't she pass away last month?

09:21.150 --> 09:25.350
They bought a pet rabbit
and named it Alice.

09:25.520 --> 09:26.720
A pet rabbit?

09:26.860 --> 09:30.320
Well, I hope the rabbit
won't end up like the girl.

09:30.660 --> 09:31.860
Hang on a second.

09:33.470 --> 09:35.830
Don't stop talking.

09:38.670 --> 09:40.830
What do you mean by
"end up like the girl"?

09:41.670 --> 09:43.730
Alice, it's time for dinner.

09:45.010 --> 09:47.140
Here we go. Eat plenty.

09:50.920 --> 09:52.750
Do you like it?

09:54.790 --> 09:55.880
What's wrong?

10:04.300 --> 10:07.030
Oh, you want some sweets.

10:07.230 --> 10:10.690
No, you can't feed her anything
besides water and vegetables!

10:11.640 --> 10:14.610
Well, she can't get
enough nutrition like that.

10:16.340 --> 10:18.610
But, she is a rabbit.

10:19.550 --> 10:22.840
What are you talking about?
Rabbits can't talk.

10:24.550 --> 10:26.040
M... Mama...

10:27.120 --> 10:29.110
She's human!!

10:29.460 --> 10:31.360
But the contract says...

10:34.560 --> 10:35.580
Daddy...

10:40.730 --> 10:42.890
Well, just one bite wouldn't hurt...

10:43.170 --> 10:45.900
Don't worry. Just this once.

10:47.240 --> 10:49.230
Here you are, Alice.
You can have it.

10:52.410 --> 10:53.400
What!?

10:56.050 --> 10:59.240
Alice was a devil
with an angel's face?

11:31.050 --> 11:34.610
I see, so they did...

11:36.960 --> 11:38.860
Yes! I knew it!

11:40.530 --> 11:43.790
Sarge! An investigation of
Chinatown is in order!

11:44.430 --> 11:46.730
Hey, that place
is sort of an extraterritoriality.

11:47.330 --> 11:49.430
You can't go in so easily.

11:50.300 --> 11:52.630
If we have proof, we can!

11:53.810 --> 11:56.870
Alice Hayward! The cause of her
death was a drug overdose!

11:57.880 --> 12:02.010
On top of that, I saw her parents
going to that pet shop!

12:02.820 --> 12:05.940
They must have bought drugs there!

12:06.320 --> 12:07.150
But...

12:07.720 --> 12:11.590
Now, I will go get proof!...Alright?

12:25.500 --> 12:27.500
Alice, sweetie...

12:31.980 --> 12:33.840
That's enough for today.

12:34.010 --> 12:36.810
Listen, too many sweets
are not good for you.

12:39.950 --> 12:41.480
Are you alright?

12:46.530 --> 12:48.750
Alice, please, stop it!

12:52.700 --> 12:55.720
I told you not to give her other foods.

12:56.030 --> 12:58.060
You said, "one bite wouldn't hurt".

13:03.910 --> 13:05.340
What's wrong, Alice?

13:05.410 --> 13:06.970
You have a stomachache?

13:16.690 --> 13:18.250
Alice? Alice!?

13:34.910 --> 13:38.070
Alice! Don't die! Alice!

13:40.080 --> 13:41.270
Mama...

13:42.580 --> 13:43.950
Mama...

13:50.020 --> 13:51.080
Mama...

13:53.890 --> 13:54.950
Mama...

13:54.990 --> 13:56.120
Mama...

13:56.360 --> 13:57.420
Mama...

13:58.460 --> 13:59.490
Mama...

14:00.570 --> 14:01.590
Mama...

14:02.900 --> 14:04.130
Mama...

14:20.050 --> 14:22.920
Count D! Just as I thought...

14:24.390 --> 14:26.950
What are you talking about?

14:28.230 --> 14:29.390
Shut up!

14:29.530 --> 14:32.260
I know you sold
drugs to their daughter!

14:32.830 --> 14:35.930
All right!
This is as good as proof!

14:37.040 --> 14:41.270
You must be joking.
I am merely the owner of a pet shop.

14:41.970 --> 14:46.040
I'm here simply to get back
the animal I sold them.

14:46.310 --> 14:48.970
I figured they wouldn't keep
to the terms of sale.

14:49.720 --> 14:52.380
However, it seems I was too late.

14:53.990 --> 14:57.890
What are you dribbling about?
You're coming with me!

15:05.660 --> 15:09.000
What's this smell?
Drugs...no, incense?

15:16.110 --> 15:17.270
What?

15:18.740 --> 15:19.730
Babies?

15:31.190 --> 15:32.490
What's happening?

15:48.940 --> 15:49.970
What is this??

15:50.110 --> 15:51.800
Was it a hallucination?

15:53.750 --> 15:55.580
You did sell them drugs!

15:55.680 --> 15:57.410
Please do not be ridiculous.

15:57.450 --> 16:00.440
This is incense bought with the rabbit
to kill the smell of drugs in this house.

16:00.490 --> 16:02.280
The rabbit dislikes the smell of drugs.

16:07.260 --> 16:08.620
Get away from me!

16:20.840 --> 16:23.810
These rabbits were eating a human?
You! What did you sell them!?

16:24.310 --> 16:30.150
What I sold was just a rabbit.
Only, it was extremely prolific.

16:54.570 --> 16:56.340
How can they increase like this?

16:56.840 --> 17:00.440
They won't stop; the city will be filled
with man-eating rabbits!

17:00.950 --> 17:03.240
Do something!
You sold them the rabbit!

17:03.620 --> 17:05.610
I did sell them a rabbit.

17:06.250 --> 17:08.580
However, it is impossible to say
which one of these it was.

17:16.060 --> 17:19.190
Besides, I have a contract with them
that we do not assume any...

17:19.230 --> 17:22.030
responsibilities if they feed the
rabbit anything other than...

17:22.070 --> 17:23.660
water and vegetables.

17:23.830 --> 17:26.570
What you need is
the Pied Piper of Hamelin.

17:55.630 --> 18:00.330
Madam, why did you break the contract
and feed her food you shouldn't have?

18:01.110 --> 18:07.010
Because...Because she wanted it.
She cried, begging for sweets.

18:08.310 --> 18:14.510
So I just gave her a piece of cookie.
She looked so happy.

18:16.020 --> 18:19.680
She smiled like an angel.

18:22.260 --> 18:26.200
Such loving creatures
human parents are.

18:29.800 --> 18:33.670
That's exactly how you killed
your daughter, the real Alice.

18:36.240 --> 18:39.040
Spoiling her to no end
since she was little,...

18:39.640 --> 18:41.810
giving her anything
and everything she wanted.

18:41.980 --> 18:44.780
Never scolding her
when she did wrong.

18:46.020 --> 18:48.610
And how did she turn out?
Withdrawn from family and society,...

18:49.820 --> 18:54.380
repeating crime after crime
and hurting others.

18:55.330 --> 18:59.020
In the end, she herself was
destroyed by drug addiction.

19:00.070 --> 19:02.730
Yet, you had a chance
to save her, did you not?

19:06.070 --> 19:09.870
Mama... Mama...
Please, give it to me.

19:11.110 --> 19:12.840
Just once, just this once!

19:13.440 --> 19:14.880
Just this once...

19:16.310 --> 19:17.750
Just this once...

19:18.750 --> 19:20.780
Yes, just this once...

19:22.020 --> 19:26.420
I didn't want her to hate me!
I loved her!

19:39.340 --> 19:42.860
These rabbits are born by tearing
their mother's womb with their teeth.

19:43.440 --> 19:47.210
The mother feeds her own
flesh and blood to her babies.

19:48.650 --> 19:52.380
The deep love of the mother itself
imposes the sin of matricide...

19:52.450 --> 19:54.010
on the children.

19:55.620 --> 20:00.110
But, still...
Still, she was my daughter!

20:05.030 --> 20:10.300
Drug addict or murderer,
she was still my daughter!!!

20:35.060 --> 20:36.360
What's happening?

20:44.500 --> 20:47.490
They're dead? How?

20:49.710 --> 20:51.700
The Piper of Hamelin played his pipe.

20:55.280 --> 20:58.840
The poison the rabbit Alice ate
finally took effect.

21:00.250 --> 21:01.310
A poison?

21:02.220 --> 21:05.250
Chocolates, candy bars,
jelly beans and cookies,...

21:06.090 --> 21:10.250
the synthetic additives in those
sweets work as deadly poison...

21:10.730 --> 21:13.160
to rabbits which are not immune.

21:14.230 --> 21:20.870
Through breeding, the additives
were slowly stored in the...

21:21.710 --> 21:24.640
rabbits' genes and then turned
into a deadly poison.

21:26.880 --> 21:32.910
Yes, what killed Alice was the love
given to her for "just this once".

21:42.090 --> 21:45.060
You knew what would happen,
didn't you?

21:47.770 --> 21:50.860
Let's get back to the shop and talk.

21:53.540 --> 21:55.400
It's about time for afternoon tea.

21:56.070 --> 22:01.210
I can serve you a delicious pie with
lots of chocolate and custard cream.
